The diffstat shows no generated root-family files. `ctlv_gen.c` and
`include/linux/ctlv_gen.h` were added in the root family patch (217219cc), and
`ctlv_gen`.o is not added to the Makefile by this patch (it only appears in the
final dispatch patch). So "Add the generated root family kernel bindings" and
"the event and generated root objects can be compile-checked here" are both
false: only event.o is built-able here, and nothing builds `ctlv_gen.c` until the
last patch. Related bisectability wart: the already-merged `include/linux/ctlv_gen.h`
uses `CTLV_EVENT_CREATE()`, which is only defined by the `ctlv_family.h` hunk of
this patch, so that header is not self-contained in patches 5-9. Either move the
macro into the patch that introduces `ctlv_gen.h` or fix the commit message.

