Summary of the most serious issues:

 - Commit message is wrong: the diff adds no generated root bindings, and
   `ctlv_gen`.o is not built until the last patch; `ctlv_gen.h` from patch 5 only
   becomes self-consistent here (`CTLV_EVENT_CREATE`).
 - `device.h` is created incomplete; patch 11 relies on fields (`transition_lock`,
   `state_generation`, `dynamic_ops_count`, disabled) that do not exist until the
   dispatch patch, so the series does not compile-check as claimed.
 - `ctlv_event_file_read()` can return `-ENODEV` just after the device-removed
   record was queued, dropping the removal notification for that read.
 - `overflow_op`/`removed_op` point into ops[] which is compacted in place later.
 - Redundant/dead checks (family `NULL`, WARN on missing root events), unused
   ctlvdev parameter, discarded validation error text, ignored emit return,
   undocumented lock ordering `transition_lock` -> `events_lock`, and the broken
   `guard()` formatting throughout.

Thanks,
Reviewer
